===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|habēn}} (Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|hebbian}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|hafa}} ({{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|hava}}/{{m|sv|ha}}), {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|habba}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|habban}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to grasp}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|hebben}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|have}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|have}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaːbən/|[ˈhaːbən]|[ˈhaːbm̩]|lang=de}} {{a|proper standard}}
* {{IPA|/ham/|lang=de}} {{a|common; particularly in the present tense, occasionally also in the infinitive}}
* {{audio|De-haben.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

